WEBVTT

cue-1
00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.580
Multiple choice is a choice-based question
type with single choice selection.

cue-2
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.740
To add a multiple choice question,

cue-3
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.620
click the Insert Content icon

cue-4
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.220
and select Multiple Choice Question.

cue-5
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.600
Make sure to edit the multiple choice
title.

cue-6
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:24.540
This is for your reference and will be
very important to the readability of our

cue-7
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:25.400
data analysis.

cue-8
00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:28.020
Students will not see the question title.

cue-9
00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:32.400
Remember to click Save after you finish
your changes to the title.

cue-10
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:37.700
Adding learning objectives to your
question follows the same process as

cue-11
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:39.380
adding learning objectives to a page.

cue-12
00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.880
In accordance with learning engineering
principles and to enable meaningful data

cue-13
00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:50.180
analysis, all questions should have at
least one associated learning objective or

cue-14
00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:51.320
sub-objective.

cue-15
00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:59.940
To begin authoring your question, in the
question text box, enter the text of the

cue-16
00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.340
question or question stem.

cue-17
00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:06.060
This will be presented to students as a
question they need to respond to.

cue-18
00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:12.720
For example, let's enter, "Which planet in
the solar system is closest to the Sun?"

cue-19
00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:21.640
The same formatting and content inserting
options available in the paragraph blocks

cue-20
00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:23.380
are available for the question stem.

cue-21
00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:29.120
Next, add the answer choices.

cue-22
00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:32.740
These are the answer options your learners
can select from.

cue-23
00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:35.840
You can add as many choices as needed.

cue-24
00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:39.840
Here, I will add three answer choices as
an example.

cue-25
00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:50.640
To add another answer choice, click Add
Choice below the existing choices.

cue-26
00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:01.280
To delete a particular answer choice,
click the X's to the right of the answer

cue-27
00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:01.660
choice.

cue-28
00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:07.260
You have two options for the order in
which students will see the answer

cue-29
00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:10.160
choices. If answer choices are shuffled,

cue-30
00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.600
students will see them in a randomly
determined order.

cue-31
00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:16.180
If answer choices are not shuffled,

cue-32
00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.600
students will see them in the order they
appear in authoring.

cue-33
00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:22.060
To select your desired option,

cue-34
00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:28.060
click the three dots menu on the far right
above the question stem.

cue-35
00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:32.840
Check or uncheck the Shuffle Answer
Choices checkbox.

cue-36
00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:42.940
To reorder the answer choices, click the
drag handle to the left of an answer

cue-37
00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:46.140
choice and drag it into the desired
position.

cue-38
00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:50.980
To set which answer choice will be marked
as correct,

cue-39
00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:53.000
go to the Answer Key tab.

cue-40
00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:58.140
Simply select the radio button next to a
correct answer.
